# Theme-shop README and Sage distribution

When prepping **README.md**, **readme.txt**, **SUPPORT.md**, or the marketplace pack for ThemeForest, TemplateMonster, Creative Market, Gumroad, or a direct sale: treat this as a **Sage 11 + Acorn + Blade + Vite 8** theme (not Bud, not a block/Gutenberg kit). Product name is **Acreline**. Install folder and text domain stay **`acreline`**. GitHub repo slug is **`wp-acreline`**.

Plugin territory, WPCS, credits, and zip contents: also follow `marketplace.mdc`.

## 1. Repository vs production zip

Git is the Sage **source**. Market buyers get a **built zip**. Do not tell a ThemeForest buyer to run `composer install` / `npm run build` on the host.

| Surface | What lives there |
| --- | --- |
| Git (`main`) | Blade, PHP, `resources/`, lockfiles. **No** `vendor/`, **no** `public/build/` |
| `acreline.zip` (`bin/build-theme-zip.sh`) | Runtime only: compiled `public/build`, production `vendor/` (`composer install --no-dev`), `style.css`, `readme.txt`, `screenshot.png` |
| Outer `acreline-*.zip` (`bin/build-install-pack.sh`) | Inner theme zip + child + Acreline Core + Documentation. Buyers extract this; they upload **inner** `acreline.zip` in wp-admin |

CI (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) publishes those zips on the `theme-latest` GitHub release. Do not commit compiled assets to git “so the zip has them.”

### `.gitignore` (keep this split)

Never commit `node_modules/` or `vendor/`. Never commit Vite output (`public/build` is covered by `/public/*` plus keep `public/images`). Dist folders stay ignored — they are build products.

Current intent (edit `.gitignore` if an agent re-opens this):

```gitignore
/node_modules
/vendor
/public/*
!/public/.gitkeep
!/public/images/
!/public/images/**
.env
.env.*
.cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
/dist-theme
/dist-marketplace
/dist-install
```

`/public/hot` and `/public/storage` are already excluded by `/public/*`. Do **not** add `!/public/build/` to git so market zips stay CI-built.

## 2. `style.css` theme header

WordPress and ThemeForest parse the comment at the top of **`style.css`**. Keep every field. Use **plain URLs**, not markdown links (`[url](url)` will fail Theme Check).

Canonical Acreline header (do **not** revert to Keystone Homes / `keystone-homes` / PHP 8.1 / WP 6.2 / Version 1.0.0):

```css
/*
Theme Name:         Acreline
Theme URI:          https://acreline.matthummel.com/
Description:        WordPress theme for farms, land, and historic homes — searchable listings, agents, and showing requests. Customizer identity and eight color styles. Blade + Tailwind + Vite (Sage 11).
Version:            1.2.3
Author:             Matt Hummel
Author URI:         https://matthummel.com/
Text Domain:        acreline
Domain Path:        /languages
License:            GNU General Public License v2 or later
License URI:        https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-2.0.html
Requires PHP:       8.3
Requires at least:  6.6
Tested up to:       7.0.1
Tags:               blog, custom-colors, custom-logo, custom-menu, featured-images, footer-widgets, theme-options, threaded-comments, translation-ready, sticky-post
*/
```

Rules when editing this header:

| Field | Keep |
| --- | --- |
| Theme Name | **Acreline** (folder is still `acreline`) |
| Theme URI | Live concept demo, not a dead GitHub slug |
| Description | Land / farms / historic homes — not “custom home builders” or generic luxury |
| Version | Must match `readme.txt` Stable tag. Bump only with a real shipping change |
| Author / Author URI | Matt Hummel / https://matthummel.com/ (not `github.com/matthummel-pa`) |
| Text Domain | **`acreline`** — same as install folder |
| License | WordPress wording (`GNU General Public License v2 or later`), not SPDX `GPL-2.0-or-later` |
| Requires PHP | **8.3** (Sage 11 / Acorn). Do not lower to 8.1 for a shop form |
| Requires at least | **6.6** |
| Tested up to | Keep in lockstep with `readme.txt` |

Child theme (`child-theme/style.css`): `Theme Name: Acreline Child`, `Template: acreline`, `Text Domain: acreline-child`.

## 3. Release zip (do not paste a yarn/Bud packager)

Shop drafts often ship a `rsync` + `yarn` + `bud.config.js` script named for **keystone-homes**. **Do not replace** this repo’s packagers with that. We already have:

| Script | What it makes |
| --- | --- |
| `bin/build-theme-zip.sh` | Inner **`dist-theme/acreline.zip`** — `npm run build`, whitelist copy, `composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader` |
| `bin/build-install-pack.sh` | Outer **`dist-install/acreline-<version>.zip`** — theme zip + `acreline-child` + Acreline Core + Documentation |
| `bin/build-marketplace-pack.sh` | Same pack plus seller brief (`SELLING.md`) in `dist-marketplace/` (repo only, not the buyer zip) |

`build-theme-zip.sh` **copies a whitelist** (`app`, `resources`, `public`, `style.css`, `readme.txt`, `screenshot.png`, `composer.lock`, …). That is stricter than “rsync everything then exclude.” Do not switch to rsync-exclude: it is easy to leak `.cursor/`, tests, and source configs into a ThemeForest zip.

Map from a typical Sage-seller paste → this repo:

| Paste said | This repo |
| --- | --- |
| `THEME_SLUG="keystone-homes"` | `SLUG="acreline"` |
| `yarn install` / `yarn build` | `npm run build` (`package-lock.json`, Node 20/22) |
| `bud.config.js` | Vite 8 (`vite.config.js`). **Keep it in git.** It is **not** in the zip because it is not on the whitelist |
| Exclude `vite.config.js` / `tailwind.config.js` from the zip | Already omitted (whitelist). Tailwind v4 lives in CSS + Vite plugin — no `tailwind.config.js` |
| Exclude `composer.lock` | **Ship `composer.lock`** in the zip, then `composer install --no-dev` in the stage dir |
| Zip to `./keystone-homes.zip` in the repo root | `dist-theme/acreline.zip` (`dist-*` is gitignored) |
| Exclude `.cursorrules` | Cursor rules are `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — never copy `.cursor/` into a buyer zip |

CI (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) runs these scripts and publishes `acreline.zip` plus the versioned seller pack on the `theme-latest` release. Do not add a second packager that writes `build/keystone-homes`.

## 4. README.md (GitHub + shops)

`README.md` is dual-audience: **zip buyers first**, Sage developers second. Do not turn it into a Keystone Homes / yarn / Bud template. Do not make `composer install` / `npm run build` the first install path.

Keep this outline (see the file):

1. One-line product (search → listings → agent → showing), then Sage in one line
2. Table: demo, support, author, **`acreline`** folder, GitHub `matthummel-pa/wp-acreline`
3. Fiction-only callout (555 phones, `@acreline-concept.test`)
4. **Install from a marketplace zip** — extract outer pack, upload inner `acreline.zip`, Identity, optional child + Core. Host: WordPress 6.6+, PHP 8.3+, no Composer/npm
5. Who it is for / what you get
6. **Local development (this git repo)** — `bin/setup-wp.sh`, then `npm run build`
7. Package scripts (`bin/build-theme-zip.sh`, `bin/build-install-pack.sh`) — versioned zip as `acreline-<version>.zip`, not a stale `1.2.0`
8. GitHub `theme-latest` updater
9. Template map
10. License GPLv2+

Also:

- Author: Matt Hummel / https://matthummel.com/
- Demo: https://acreline.matthummel.com/
- Buyer walkthrough lives in `docs/marketplace/`; start at **`docs/marketplace/index.html`**. Do not paste that HTML into README. Pack script copies the whole hub (`index`, buyer-guide, branding, requirements, support, sources, changelog, `assets/`, `screenshots/`) into `Documentation/`. Do not shrink the pack back to three HTML files.
- Do **not** claim WordPress.org approval, Gutenberg-optimized, Elementor, or a live IDX/MLS
- Do **not** paste Envato item IDs or dummy license keys
- Support: `SUPPORT.md` and GitHub issues on `matthummel-pa/wp-acreline`

## 5. readme.txt (WP.org / ThemeForest parser)

`readme.txt` is the **store parser** file (Stable tag, Requires at least, Tested up to, Requires PHP, License GPLv2+, tags). Keep it in WP.org format even if we are not submitting yet.

- Stable tag matches `style.css` Version
- Description: land, farms, historic homes — not generic luxury brokerage
- Installation: upload **`acreline.zip`**, folder name `acreline`, Customize → Identity, optional Seed + Core + child
- FAQ: phone in Customizer; demo banner off; listings are a CPT (Core or theme fallback)
- Changelog: user-facing, short; no agent jargon
- Resources: fonts and licenses (see `CREDITS.md`)

## 6. Copy you can paste on the store listing

Use `docs/marketplace/themeforest-listing.md` and `requirements.html` as the source of truth for ThemeForest / TemplateMonster form fields (software version, browsers, Gutenberg optimized = **No**, WooCommerce/WPML/RTL = No, demo URL, support URL, license). Short description lives there too. Screenshots for extra item images: `docs/marketplace/screenshots/`. Sources: `docs/marketplace/sources.html`. WordPress.org upload rules: `docs/marketplace/wordpress-org.md`. Buyer HTML starts at `docs/marketplace/index.html`. Do not invent a second set of versions in README that disagrees with `style.css` / `readme.txt`.

## Do not

- Commit `vendor/` or `public/build/` to git to “help ThemeForest”
- Tell buyers this is a Bud or Sage 10 theme
- Lead README with `yarn` / `composer install` as the shop install path
- Enable the block editor or Gutenberg patterns to pass a shop checklist
- Put `SELLING.md` inside the buyer zip
- Rename the install folder away from `acreline` in README “for branding”
